# coupling-hand.xrs - does the hand/weapon MODEL follow the controller, and does
# the AIM stay in sync with it while the controller moves?
#
# The head is held perfectly still throughout, so anything that changes in these
# captures was caused by the controller and nothing else. That is the whole point
# of a simulated headset: a human cannot hold their head still.
#
# Two questions, two oracles:
#
# 1. DOES THE MODEL FOLLOW THE CONTROLLER?
#    img-diff consecutive captures. With the head static, a model that tracks the
#    controller produces a large, LOCALISED change (use -Grid 16 and look at the
#    bbox); a model that ignores the controller produces almost nothing.
#      .\tools\img-diff.ps1 -A hand_c_left.png -B hand_r_left.png -Grid 16
#
# 2. IS THE AIM IN SYNC WITH THE MODEL?
#    Numeric, no eyeballing: $s.AimRayMaxDev is the worst angular deviation of the
#    aim-laser dots from the ray leaving the hand. It should stay near zero at
#    EVERY controller position. If it grows as the controller swings out, the aim
#    and the model have drifted apart - the gun points somewhere other than where
#    it shoots.
#      $shots | ForEach-Object { $_.AimRayMaxDev }
#
# BOTH subsystems must be armed or the test answers the wrong question:
#   vrhands drives the MODEL   -> question 1
#   vraim   drives the RAY     -> question 2
# Arming only vraim was the first version of this file, and it "passed" with the
# image barely changing - because nothing was moving the model at all.
#
# Stereo is armed HERE rather than left to the caller. Testing mono has misled
# this project before (sessions 12-13), and `vrstereo on` is sticky, so a
# sequence that assumes someone else armed it will silently run flat one day.
reset
@mod vrstereo on
@mod vrhands on; vraim on; vraim laser on
@frames 60
@assert projectionViews eq 2
# Detach the hand from the head and place it centred in front of the face, then
# sweep it. `hand to` interpolates, so the model is seen tracking across frames
# rather than teleporting.
hand r grip pose 0.20 1.30 -0.45 0 0 0
@frames 20
@shot hand_c
@assert layersLastFrame ge 3
hand r to grip 0.55 1.30 -0.45 -25 0 0 400
@frames 40
@shot hand_r
hand r to grip -0.15 1.30 -0.45 25 0 0 400
@frames 40
@shot hand_l
hand r to grip 0.20 1.05 -0.45 0 -25 0 400
@frames 40
@shot hand_down
hand r to grip 0.20 1.55 -0.45 0 25 0 400
@frames 40
@shot hand_up
